1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,664
TEO (V.O.): What does a man look like... when

2
00:00:02,364 --> 00:00:04,000
TEO (V.O.): he succeeds completely at

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,765
TEO (V.O.): everything his world asks of him?

4
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:07,354
NOA: Okay.

5
00:00:07,314 --> 00:00:08,330
NOA: Hear me out.

6
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:11,076
NOA: David, then Solomon, then Jesus.

7
00:00:11,036 --> 00:00:11,997
NOA: It's one arc.

8
00:00:11,997 --> 00:00:14,492
NOA: David's the emotional, musical one.

9
00:00:14,452 --> 00:00:16,650
NOA: Chill... unless he's defending somebody.

10
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:18,504
TEO: Your arc holds together.

11
00:00:18,464 --> 00:00:20,354
TEO: Honestly, better than you think.

12
00:00:20,554 --> 00:00:21,976
TEO: But one piece needs an

13
00:00:21,676 --> 00:00:23,200
TEO: honest correction first.

14
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:24,401
NOA: Which piece?

15
00:00:24,501 --> 00:00:26,205
TEO: Chill unless defending.

16
00:00:26,165 --> 00:00:28,497
TEO: The record is much more violent than that.

17
00:00:28,697 --> 00:00:30,229
TEO: And including the violence

18
00:00:29,929 --> 00:00:31,366
TEO: makes your arc stronger.

19
00:00:31,326 --> 00:00:32,252
TEO: Not weaker.

20
00:00:32,652 --> 00:00:33,510
NOA: Show me.

21
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:36,057
TEO (V.O.): You're right that he was gifted.

22
00:00:36,017 --> 00:00:38,256
TEO (V.O.): He played music for a troubled king.

23
00:00:38,356 --> 00:00:40,388
TEO (V.O.): He loved his friend Jonathan with a

24
00:00:40,088 --> 00:00:41,674
TEO (V.O.): bond deeper than brothers.

25
00:00:41,774 --> 00:00:43,560
DAVID: I will dance before the Lord!

26
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:45,043
DAVID: I will become even more

27
00:00:44,743 --> 00:00:46,212
DAVID: undignified than this!

28
00:00:46,312 --> 00:00:48,365
TEO (V.O.): He danced with everything he had.

29
00:00:48,325 --> 00:00:49,217
TEO (V.O.): And he wept.

30
00:00:49,177 --> 00:00:49,907
TEO (V.O.): Openly.

31
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:50,968
TEO (V.O.): Without shame.

32
00:00:51,168 --> 00:00:52,715
DAVID: How long, O Lord?

33
00:00:52,675 --> 00:00:54,376
DAVID: Will you forget me forever?

34
00:00:54,876 --> 00:00:57,534
WOMEN: Saul has struck down his thousands...

35
00:00:57,234 --> 00:00:59,382
WOMEN: and David, his ten thousands!

36
00:00:59,582 --> 00:01:01,763
TEO (V.O.): His society rewarded him for killing.

37
00:01:01,723 --> 00:01:03,694
TEO (V.O.): And they sang about it in the streets.

38
00:01:04,294 --> 00:01:06,406
TEO (V.O.): Living among the Philistines,

39
00:01:06,106 --> 00:01:09,529
TEO (V.O.): he raided towns... and left no man or woman alive.

40
00:01:09,829 --> 00:01:11,461
TEO (V.O.): So that no survivor could

41
00:01:11,161 --> 00:01:12,741
TEO (V.O.): report what he had done.

42
00:01:13,541 --> 00:01:16,130
TEO (V.O.): He took Bathsheba, the wife of Uriah,

43
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:17,986
TEO (V.O.): one of his own loyal soldiers.

44
00:01:18,186 --> 00:01:19,607
DAVID: Set Uriah in the front of

45
00:01:19,307 --> 00:01:20,548
DAVID: the hardest fighting.

46
00:01:20,508 --> 00:01:22,078
DAVID: Then draw back from him,

47
00:01:21,778 --> 00:01:23,454
DAVID: so that he is struck down.

48
00:01:23,654 --> 00:01:25,614
TEO (V.O.): Uriah carried the letter himself.

49
00:01:25,574 --> 00:01:28,452
TEO (V.O.): His own death, sealed, in his hand.

50
00:01:29,452 --> 00:01:31,822
TEO (V.O.): Over an insult, he set out to kill

51
00:01:31,522 --> 00:01:33,954
TEO (V.O.): Nabal, and every male in his house.

52
00:01:34,054 --> 00:01:35,473
ABIGAIL: My lord, please.

53
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:37,074
ABIGAIL: Do not carry the guilt of

54
00:01:36,774 --> 00:01:38,628
ABIGAIL: shedding blood without cause.

55
00:01:39,028 --> 00:01:40,467
DAVID: Blessed be your wisdom.

56
00:01:40,427 --> 00:01:42,487
DAVID: You kept me this day from bloodguilt.

57
00:01:42,587 --> 00:01:44,202
TEO (V.O.): He stopped only because a

58
00:01:43,902 --> 00:01:45,464
TEO (V.O.): woman stood in the road.

59
00:01:46,164 --> 00:01:47,435
DAVID: My son.

60
00:01:47,395 --> 00:01:50,532
DAVID: I wanted to build a house for God.

61
00:01:50,632 --> 00:01:53,478
DAVID: But God said to me: you shall not build it...

62
00:01:53,178 --> 00:01:55,346
DAVID: because you have shed much blood.

63
00:01:56,146 --> 00:01:57,106
DAVID: Joab.

64
00:01:57,066 --> 00:01:59,163
DAVID: Do not let his gray head go

65
00:01:58,863 --> 00:02:00,961
DAVID: down to the grave in peace.

66
00:02:01,161 --> 00:02:03,335
DAVID: And Shimei... bring his gray

67
00:02:03,035 --> 00:02:04,741
DAVID: head down with blood.

68
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:06,943
TEO (V.O.): Even dying, the sword was the

69
00:02:06,643 --> 00:02:08,545
TEO (V.O.): last thing he handed his son.

70
00:02:09,545 --> 00:02:11,116
NOA: So... he wasn't chill.

71
00:02:11,316 --> 00:02:13,799
TEO: He did exactly what his society told him.

72
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:15,510
TEO: And he was excellent at it.

73
00:02:15,610 --> 00:02:17,779
TEO: What it told him included killing.

74
00:02:17,739 --> 00:02:18,957
TEO: And people cheered.

75
00:02:19,457 --> 00:02:21,718
NOA: So David is what it looks like... when

76
00:02:21,418 --> 00:02:23,318
NOA: someone wins the whole program.

77
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:24,596
TEO: Completely.

78
00:02:24,556 --> 00:02:26,243
TEO: And then... there's the kid who

79
00:02:25,943 --> 00:02:27,317
TEO: grew up inside that win.

80
00:02:28,117 --> 00:02:30,314
TEO (V.O.): Solomon was born to Bathsheba

81
00:02:30,014 --> 00:02:31,819
TEO (V.O.): after Uriah was killed.

82
00:02:31,779 --> 00:02:33,460
TEO (V.O.): Their first child had died.

83
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:35,884
TEO (V.O.): He grew up in a house where his brother

84
00:02:35,584 --> 00:02:37,315
TEO (V.O.): Amnon raped his sister Tamar.

85
00:02:37,515 --> 00:02:39,824
TEO (V.O.): Where Absalom killed Amnon for it.

86
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:41,312
TEO (V.O.): Then rebelled against their

87
00:02:41,012 --> 00:02:42,812
TEO (V.O.): father... and died in the revolt.

88
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:44,353
DAVID: O my son Absalom!

89
00:02:44,313 --> 00:02:45,955
DAVID: My son, my son!

90
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:48,225
DAVID: If only I had died instead of you!

91
00:02:48,525 --> 00:02:50,602
TEO (V.O.): On the surface: a palace.

92
00:02:50,562 --> 00:02:52,023
TEO (V.O.): A beloved king.

93
00:02:51,983 --> 00:02:52,712
TEO (V.O.): Wealth.

94
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:54,006
TEO (V.O.): God's favor.

95
00:02:54,006 --> 00:02:56,122
TEO (V.O.): Underneath: a father brilliant in

96
00:02:55,822 --> 00:02:57,884
TEO (V.O.): public... who could not stop the

97
00:02:57,584 --> 00:02:59,646
TEO (V.O.): destruction inside his own home.

98
00:02:59,946 --> 00:03:01,620
YOUNG SOLOMON: Something's wrong here.

99
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,549
YOUNG SOLOMON: And nobody will say what it is.

100
00:03:04,149 --> 00:03:05,877
TEO (V.O.): Then Solomon got everything.

101
00:03:05,837 --> 00:03:08,285
TEO (V.O.): At a scale nobody else ever got.

102
00:03:08,285 --> 00:03:09,096
TEO (V.O.): Wisdom.

103
00:03:09,056 --> 00:03:09,786
TEO (V.O.): Wealth.

104
00:03:09,746 --> 00:03:10,684
TEO (V.O.): Buildings.

105
00:03:10,644 --> 00:03:11,618
TEO (V.O.): Gardens.

106
00:03:11,518 --> 00:03:13,106
TEO (V.O.): Seven hundred wives.

107
00:03:13,066 --> 00:03:14,922
TEO (V.O.): Three hundred concubines.

108
00:03:14,822 --> 00:03:16,132
TEO (V.O.): Forced labor.

109
00:03:16,092 --> 00:03:17,576
TEO (V.O.): International fame.

110
00:03:17,676 --> 00:03:19,071
TEO (V.O.): If more were the answer,

111
00:03:18,771 --> 00:03:21,215
TEO (V.O.): he would have been the happiest man in history.

112
00:03:22,115 --> 00:03:24,020
SOLOMON: Vanity of vanities.

113
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:25,599
SOLOMON: All is vanity.

114
00:03:25,899 --> 00:03:27,708
TEO (V.O.): The Hebrew word is hevel.

115
00:03:27,668 --> 00:03:28,467
TEO (V.O.): Vapor.

116
00:03:28,427 --> 00:03:29,099
TEO (V.O.): Breath.

117
00:03:29,059 --> 00:03:30,497
TEO (V.O.): Something you can't grab.

118
00:03:30,597 --> 00:03:32,713
SOLOMON: I made great works.

119
00:03:32,673 --> 00:03:34,281
SOLOMON: I built houses.

120
00:03:34,241 --> 00:03:36,682
SOLOMON: I planted vineyards for myself...

121
00:03:36,582 --> 00:03:39,063
SOLOMON: and behold, all was vanity,

122
00:03:38,763 --> 00:03:41,163
SOLOMON: and a striving after wind.

123
00:03:41,663 --> 00:03:43,392
SOLOMON: So I hated life.

124
00:03:43,692 --> 00:03:46,001
TEO (V.O.): Tradition says Solomon wrote it.

125
00:03:45,961 --> 00:03:47,665
TEO (V.O.): Many scholars think a later

126
00:03:47,365 --> 00:03:48,966
TEO (V.O.): writer took on his voice.

127
00:03:48,926 --> 00:03:51,060
TEO (V.O.): Either way... it's the report from the top.

128
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:54,312
SOLOMON: There is one who has no other.

129
00:03:54,272 --> 00:03:55,343
SOLOMON: No son.

130
00:03:55,303 --> 00:03:56,508
SOLOMON: No brother.

131
00:03:56,468 --> 00:03:59,880
SOLOMON: Yet there is no end to all his toil... and his

132
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:02,384
SOLOMON: eyes are never satisfied with riches.

133
00:04:02,884 --> 00:04:04,637
SOLOMON: Two are better than one.

134
00:04:04,737 --> 00:04:06,167
SOLOMON: For if they fall,

135
00:04:05,867 --> 00:04:08,027
SOLOMON: one will lift up his fellow.

136
00:04:08,227 --> 00:04:11,271
SOLOMON: But woe to him who is alone when he falls,

137
00:04:10,971 --> 00:04:13,557
SOLOMON: and has not another to lift him up.

138
00:04:13,757 --> 00:04:16,717
SOLOMON: If two lie together, they keep warm.

139
00:04:16,677 --> 00:04:19,005
SOLOMON: But how can one keep warm alone?

140
00:04:19,405 --> 00:04:22,595
SOLOMON: A threefold cord is not quickly broken.

141
00:04:23,595 --> 00:04:25,123
NOA: That's... the door test.

142
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:28,167
TEO: The man with everything says the emptiness is

143
00:04:27,867 --> 00:04:30,341
TEO: endless toil, with nobody beside you.

144
00:04:30,441 --> 00:04:32,993
TEO: Woe to him who is alone when he falls.

145
00:04:32,953 --> 00:04:34,685
TEO: That's the person on the floor...

146
00:04:34,385 --> 00:04:35,900
TEO: with zero doors to knock on.

147
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:37,269
NOA: Yeah.

148
00:04:37,229 --> 00:04:38,526
NOA: I know that floor.

149
00:04:38,926 --> 00:04:40,120
TEO: I know you do.

150
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,143
TEO: Now watch what the Son of

151
00:04:41,843 --> 00:04:43,467
TEO: David does with all this.

152
00:04:44,267 --> 00:04:46,599
TEO (V.O.): They called Jesus the Son of David.

153
00:04:46,559 --> 00:04:48,937
TEO (V.O.): And he talked about Solomon directly.

154
00:04:49,037 --> 00:04:50,927
JESUS: Consider the lilies of the field.

155
00:04:50,887 --> 00:04:52,807
JESUS: Even Solomon in all his glory was

156
00:04:52,507 --> 00:04:54,279
JESUS: not dressed like one of these.

157
00:04:54,479 --> 00:04:56,684
JESUS: Something greater than Solomon is here.

158
00:04:57,284 --> 00:04:59,360
TEO (V.O.): From David, he kept the heart.

159
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,282
TEO (V.O.): The music.

160
00:05:00,242 --> 00:05:01,261
TEO (V.O.): The raw prayer.

161
00:05:01,221 --> 00:05:02,915
TEO (V.O.): The loyalty of a friend.

162
00:05:03,015 --> 00:05:04,659
PETER: Lord, should we strike with the sword?

163
00:05:04,859 --> 00:05:06,609
JESUS: Put your sword back in its place.

164
00:05:06,809 --> 00:05:07,979
JESUS: Love your enemies.

165
00:05:07,939 --> 00:05:09,734
JESUS: Pray for those who persecute you.

166
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:12,463
TEO (V.O.): David's heart... with David's sword removed.

167
00:05:13,163 --> 00:05:15,298
TEO (V.O.): From Solomon, he took the proof.

168
00:05:15,258 --> 00:05:16,861
TEO (V.O.): That experiment had already

169
00:05:16,561 --> 00:05:18,019
TEO (V.O.): been run to the maximum.

170
00:05:18,119 --> 00:05:20,167
JESUS: Do not store up treasures on earth.

171
00:05:20,127 --> 00:05:21,492
JESUS: Go, sell what you have,

172
00:05:21,192 --> 00:05:22,510
JESUS: and come... follow me.

173
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:23,948
TEO (V.O.): More wealth.

174
00:05:23,908 --> 00:05:25,207
TEO (V.O.): More buildings.

175
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:26,268
TEO (V.O.): More achievement.

176
00:05:26,228 --> 00:05:28,008
TEO (V.O.): It ended in 'I hated life.'

177
00:05:27,708 --> 00:05:29,105
TEO (V.O.): He didn't repeat it.

178
00:05:29,905 --> 00:05:32,443
TEO (V.O.): Instead of a palace, he built this.

179
00:05:32,403 --> 00:05:34,224
TEO (V.O.): Twelve people walking together.

180
00:05:34,184 --> 00:05:35,262
TEO (V.O.): Eating together.

181
00:05:35,222 --> 00:05:36,997
TEO (V.O.): Sleeping outside together.

182
00:05:37,097 --> 00:05:38,418
TEO (V.O.): Shared meals.

183
00:05:38,378 --> 00:05:39,665
TEO (V.O.): A shared purse.

184
00:05:39,625 --> 00:05:40,761
TEO (V.O.): Touching lepers.

185
00:05:40,721 --> 00:05:42,263
TEO (V.O.): Eating with outcasts.

186
00:05:42,263 --> 00:05:43,820
TEO (V.O.): A group where nobody was

187
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:44,920
TEO (V.O.): alone when they fell.

188
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,424
JESUS: Love one another, as I have loved you.

189
00:05:47,724 --> 00:05:49,556
JESUS: Where two or three are gathered in my

190
00:05:49,256 --> 00:05:50,716
JESUS: name, there I am among them.

191
00:05:50,916 --> 00:05:51,796
TEO (V.O.): Two. Three.

192
00:05:51,756 --> 00:05:53,241
TEO (V.O.): A threefold cord.

193
00:05:53,201 --> 00:05:54,522
TEO (V.O.): A village... embodied.

194
00:05:55,322 --> 00:05:57,481
NOA: A cord of three... instead of a crown.

195
00:05:57,681 --> 00:05:59,815
TEO: A table instead of a palace.

196
00:06:02,115 --> 00:06:02,915
AMI: Hey.

197
00:06:02,875 --> 00:06:04,231
AMI: I didn't call first.

198
00:06:04,191 --> 00:06:05,861
AMI: Is that okay?

199
00:06:06,261 --> 00:06:07,708
NOA: It's more than okay.

200
00:06:07,668 --> 00:06:08,508
NOA: Come in.

201
00:06:09,608 --> 00:06:10,930
TEO (V.O.): Two are better than one.

202
00:06:10,890 --> 00:06:12,518
TEO (V.O.): And a threefold cord... is

203
00:06:12,218 --> 00:06:13,489
TEO (V.O.): not quickly broken.
